<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>PreferenceSpecifiers</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSGroupSpecifier</string>
			<key>FooterText</key>
			<string>Opens the app straight to the settings menu. Useful if you changed anything there and need to change it back but the app won&apos;t start.</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSToggleSwitchSpecifier</string>
			<key>Title</key>
			<string>Recovery Mode</string>
			<key>Key</key>
			<string>recovery</string>
			<key>DefaultValue</key>
			<false/>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSToggleSwitchSpecifier</string>
			<key>Title</key>
			<string>Open Diagnostics On Launch</string>
			<key>Key</key>
			<string>openDiagnosticsOnLaunch</string>
			<key>DefaultValue</key>
			<false/>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSMultiValueSpecifier</string>
			<key>Title</key>
			<string>Initial Window</string>
			<key>Key</key>
			<string>Initial Window</string>
			<key>DefaultValue</key>
			<string>terminal</string>
			<key>Titles</key>
			<array>
				<string>Workspace</string>
				<string>Choose Filesystem</string>
				<string>Terminal (tty1)</string>
				<string>Session Shell (pts/1)</string>
			</array>
			<key>Values</key>
			<array>
				<string>workspace</string>
				<string>choose-filesystem</string>
				<string>terminal</string>
				<string>session-shell</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSGroupSpecifier</string>
			<key>Title</key>
			<string>Simulated Swap</string>
			<key>FooterText</key>
			<string>Lets iSH-AOK move cold guest memory out to storage, so a large mostly-idle heap or a background process tree stops counting against the memory iOS allows the app. It will not make a working set that is genuinely too big run well.

Off unless you turn it on: swapping writes to the device&apos;s flash, and the swap area takes up that much space in the app&apos;s container while it exists. Both settings take effect the next time iSH-AOK starts, and swap stays off until you have chosen a size as well as switched it on.

The sizes offered here do not know how much room this device actually has. If there is not enough free space for the size you pick, iSH-AOK leaves swap off rather than quietly making a smaller area than you asked for; &quot;cat /proc/ish/swap&quot; in the guest says which of those happened.</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSToggleSwitchSpecifier</string>
			<key>Title</key>
			<string>Enable Swap</string>
			<key>Key</key>
			<string>Enable Swap</string>
			<key>DefaultValue</key>
			<false/>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSMultiValueSpecifier</string>
			<key>Title</key>
			<string>Swap Size</string>
			<key>Key</key>
			<string>Swap Size MB</string>
			<key>DefaultValue</key>
			<integer>0</integer>
			<key>Titles</key>
			<array>
				<string>Not chosen (swap stays off)</string>
				<string>256 MB</string>
				<string>512 MB</string>
				<string>1 GB</string>
				<string>2 GB</string>
				<string>4 GB</string>
				<string>8 GB</string>
				<string>16 GB</string>
			</array>
			<key>Values</key>
			<array>
				<integer>0</integer>
				<integer>256</integer>
				<integer>512</integer>
				<integer>1024</integer>
				<integer>2048</integer>
				<integer>4096</integer>
				<integer>8192</integer>
				<integer>16384</integer>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSGroupSpecifier</string>
			<key>Title</key>
			<string>Compressed Memory</string>
			<key>FooterText</key>
			<string>Holds cold memory compressed in RAM instead of writing it to storage. Measured 2.2–2.8x on real workloads, so a 128 MB pool holds roughly 300 MB of guest memory, and a page comes back about two orders of magnitude faster than a read from flash.

Works on its own — Swap is NOT required, and with Swap off nothing is ever written to storage at all. If Swap is also on, this sits in front of it and only what does not compress reaches the file.

Uses the RAM you give it, and it counts against the same memory limit the guest does — so a pool bigger than the device can spare makes things worse, not better. Anything above a quarter of this device's memory is reduced to that.</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSToggleSwitchSpecifier</string>
			<key>Title</key>
			<string>Enable Compressed Memory</string>
			<key>Key</key>
			<string>Enable Compressed Memory</string>
			<key>DefaultValue</key>
			<false/>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSMultiValueSpecifier</string>
			<key>Title</key>
			<string>Compressed Memory Size</string>
			<key>Key</key>
			<string>Compressed Memory Size MB</string>
			<key>DefaultValue</key>
			<integer>128</integer>
			<key>Titles</key>
			<array>
				<string>Off</string>
				<string>32 MB</string>
				<string>64 MB</string>
				<string>128 MB</string>
				<string>256 MB</string>
				<string>512 MB</string>
				<string>1 GB</string>
				<string>2 GB</string>
				<string>4 GB</string>
			</array>
			<key>Values</key>
			<array>
				<integer>0</integer>
				<integer>32</integer>
				<integer>64</integer>
				<integer>128</integer>
				<integer>256</integer>
				<integer>512</integer>
				<integer>1024</integer>
				<integer>2048</integer>
				<integer>4096</integer>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
